# AXIS CELL: consumer = the `EMatch` (expression-match) `safety_commit` JOIN.
# The program is the SMatch join cell `n2_nested_uam.gg` rewritten so the match
# is an EXPRESSION, which routes the commit through a DIFFERENT consumer of the
# same classifier.
#
# ⚠ `n2_nested_uam.gg` CANNOT see a weakening applied only here, and the
# converse holds too — measured. An earlier version of this net omitted an
# EMatch cell on the reasoning that "an EMatch-only route must edit the `:2671`
# call text, which the argument pin sees". That reasoning is FALSE for a
# SUBSTRING pin: `and`-extending the argument appends text after the substring
# and leaves a `grep -c` unchanged. (This tree's pin compares the WHOLE trimmed
# line, so it does fire — but the cell is what makes the guarantee independent
# of how the pin happens to be written.)
#
# `Outer.Wrap` and `Outer.Nil` are every variant of `Outer`, but the `Wrap` arm
# only matches payload `Inner.Red()`. `main` passes `Outer.Wrap(Inner.Blue())`,
# so control falls out of the match with `s` still moved and `print(s)` is a
# use-after-move — rejected by `gg check` with `error[E_UseAfterMove]`.
#
# ⚠ SPELLING IS LOAD-BEARING: all-`PConstructor` top-level arms, no prelude
# variant — see the note in `n2_nested_uam.gg`.
#
# RED-VERIFY (weaken THIS consumer only): `and`-extend the EMatch join's
# argument with a separate exhaustiveness helper —
#   `safety_commit(em_acc, not match_has_catch_all(arms) and not <helper>(arms),
#                  em_reached, &state)`
# leaving the `SMatch` join untouched — and rebuild the driver. Measured: this
# cell flips rc 1 -> rc 0, 7296 bytes of C, while `n2_nested_uam.gg` — the same
# program shape through the statement form — stays GREEN.
enum Inner:
    Red()
    Blue()

enum Outer:
    Wrap(Inner)
    Nil()

void sink(String ^x):
    pass

int probe(Outer o):
    String s = "hello"
    sink(^s)
    int n = match o:
        case Outer.Wrap(Inner.Red()):
            s = "a"
            1
        case Outer.Nil():
            s = "b"
            2
    print(s)
    return n

void main():
    print(probe(Outer.Wrap(Inner.Blue())))
